{
  "description": "Shapes and errors that more than one API area uses. The spec declares no errors, so every failure surfaced as a bare status class or UnknownResendError. Each class here matches Resend's machine-readable `name` (core's matcher `code` is numeric, so the name is matched as `body: {\"/name\": ...}`), with the status and, where one name covers several cases, the message, from Resend's error reference (api-reference/errors) and a live run (2026-10-29): the auth and validation errors every operation gets, idempotency, the sending quota, sender and recipient errors, and the not-founds of resources several areas address. The quota errors carry no httpError, so they get no throttling category and the default retry policy does not wait out a quota that resets at midnight; rate_limit_exceeded stays core's retried TooManyRequests. Each area file attaches these to its operations. Response members are narrowed to what Resend returns: required where resend-node, the maintained official SDK, declares them non-optional and every live response (2026-10-29) carried them, and nullable where resend-node allows null or a live response held null. That applies here to attachments (sent and received mail) and contact listings (contacts and segments).",
